Machine Vision Academy Open Academic Licence (MVA-OAL)

CREATION AND PUBLICATION NOTICE

This document is provided as the governing licence text for Machine Vision Academy materials. It is intended to define the permitted public use of the work and the restrictions that apply to it.

Statement of Purpose

Machine Vision Academy exists to share high-quality educational material for machine vision, computer vision and artificial intelligence in support of public, non-profit and state-funded education. The purpose of this licence is to allow the widest possible educational use while protecting the work from commercial exploitation and unauthorised redistribution.

1. Core Permissions (What is Allowed)

This content is free to use, display and distribute strictly for public, non-profit, state-funded educational institutions, such as public universities, community colleges and public schools, for instructional, academic and research purposes.

2. Mandatory Attribution Clause

Any public educational institution sharing, displaying or distributing this content in its original form must clearly acknowledge authorship by including the following visible text and a live, clickable hyperlink on every digital or physical medium where the content appears:

Source: Machine Vision Academy. Original content available at machinevisionacademy.org.

3. Derivative Works and Section Usage

If an eligible public institution extracts sections, chapters, images or snippets of this content to incorporate into its own custom course packs, lecture slides or internal materials, it must follow both of the following conditions:

* Academic Citation: It must formally cite the author and title of the handbook following standard academic publication guidelines, such as APA, IEEE or Harvard style.
* Prior Written Consent: It must obtain formal, explicit written permission from the administrator of machinevisionacademy.org before publishing or distributing the modified material.

4. Commercial and Private Restrictions (What is Forbidden)

This licence strictly excludes any commercial, for-profit or private corporate use.

You are completely prohibited from copying, distributing, adapting or hosting this content on websites, internal databases or training platforms if you are:

* A private, for-profit educational institution, private college or commercial training company.
* A commercial business, corporation or vendor operating within the machine vision, automation, robotics or hardware industries.
* Any entity attempting to use this material for direct or indirect commercial profit, marketing or lead generation.

5. Violation and Rights Reservation

Any unauthorised use of this material by restricted entities, or any failure to provide proper attribution and secure written consent by public entities, constitutes an infringement of copyright. The authors and rights holders reserve all legal rights to demand immediate removal of the content and to seek remedies under applicable intellectual property law.

No Warranty

This work is provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied. The authors make no representation that the content is complete, error-free or suitable for any particular purpose.
